34. Connect this to your Java experience
Here's how your existing knowledge maps to distributed theory:
Java / backend concept	Distributed-systems equivalent
Thread	Process/node
Shared memory	No equivalent across nodes
synchronized	Distributed coordination problem
Lock	Distributed lock / consensus-related coordination
Method call	Network message/RPC
Exception	Communication/process failure
Timeout	Failure suspicion, not proof
GC pause	Node appears unavailable
JVM crash	Process crash
Multiple JVMs	Replicated/distributed processes
DB replication	Distributed state
Transaction	Distributed atomicity problem
volatile	Not a distributed consistency mechanism
ConcurrentHashMap	Local concurrency only
Load balancer	Request distribution
Kafka/RabbitMQ	Asynchronous message communication
This distinction is particularly important:
Concurrency
    ↓
multiple threads
    ↓
shared memory
versus:
Distribution
    ↓
multiple processes/machines
    ↓
message passing
    ↓
independent failure
Concurrency and distribution overlap, but they are not the same problem.
