That's too simplistic.
The more useful mental model is:
A participant cannot always distinguish "the operation did not happen" from "the operation happened but its acknowledgement was lost."
That uncertainty creates the duplicate problem.
And this occurs everywhere:
•	HTTP 
•	RPC 
•	message queues 
•	Kafka 
•	databases 
•	payment systems 
•	distributed jobs 
