19. What Kafka changes — and what it doesn't
Kafka provides powerful mechanisms around:
•	durable logs 
•	offsets 
•	consumer groups 
•	retries 
•	producer idempotence 
•	transactions 
But Kafka cannot magically guarantee:
Kafka
  ↓
your Java code
  ↓
Oracle/PostgreSQL
  ↓
external REST API
  ↓
email provider
all behave exactly once.
For example:
Kafka transaction
      ↓
Java application
      ↓
HTTP POST /charge-card
