20. The mental model I want you to carry forward
Don't think:
Exactly once = message arrives once
Think:
Exactly once
      |
      +── delivery
      |
      +── execution
      |
      +── state transition
      |
      +── external side effect
Each layer has different failure modes.
A distributed system may have:
delivery       = twice
execution      = twice
database effect = once
external effect = twice
That isn't contradictory.
It's why "exactly once" without specifying the boundary of the guarantee is almost meaningless.
