21. A production-grade way to phrase guarantees
Instead of saying:
"Our system is exactly once."
A serious distributed-systems engineer should say something like:
"Kafka processing is transactional and offsets are committed atomically with Kafka output, while writes to PostgreSQL use an idempotency key. Therefore the database business effect is effectively once per operation, assuming the idempotency record and business mutation share the same local transaction."
That statement has boundaries.
And boundaries are everything in distributed systems.
