35. Why Kafka transactions alone aren't enough for payments
Suppose:
Kafka → Payment Service
Your Java consumer:
BEGIN Kafka TX
   ↓
call payment API
   ↓
payment succeeds
   ↓
Kafka output
   ↓
commit transaction
Now:
payment succeeds
but:
CRASH before Kafka commit
On retry:
call payment API again
Kafka transaction can't undo the first payment.
So:
Kafka exactly-once
doesn't imply:
payment exactly-once
The payment API itself needs an idempotency mechanism or another transactional strategy.
And that brings us directly to Lesson 4.
