31. Idempotency key lifetime matters
Suppose you store:
P123
for only 5 minutes.
After expiration:
P123
may become valid again.
Is that safe?
Depends on the business semantics.
For payments, you may need a much longer retention period.
For some internal commands, a shorter window may be sufficient.
So:
Idempotency isn't just an algorithm; it has a retention and business-identity model.
