32. The "exactly once" illusion
Suppose we build:
Kafka
 ↓
Java
 ↓
PostgreSQL
with:
Kafka at-least-once
+
Postgres idempotency
We can say:
"The PostgreSQL business effect is effectively exactly once per operation."
But don't say:
"The entire system is exactly once."
Why?
Because another side effect may exist:
PostgreSQL
 ↓
send email
Now:
DB commit
 ↓
email
 ↓
CRASH
Retry:
email
twice.
The DB was exactly-once.
The email wasn't.
This is the bridge to Lesson 5.
