37. But even the outbox relay can publish twice
Suppose:
Outbox relay
   |
   | publish event
   ↓
Kafka
   |
   | success
   ↓
CRASH
Relay hasn't marked the outbox row as published.
It retries:
same event
So Kafka may receive:
event
event
Unless the Kafka side uses an appropriate mechanism.
This is another beautiful example of:
You don't eliminate every duplicate. You make duplicates safe.
