38. Exactly-once is therefore compositional
This is the deeper idea.
Imagine:
A → B → C → D
For each boundary:
A→B : idempotency
B→C : transaction
C→D : deduplication
You can construct a system where the business effect is exactly once even though individual operations may be retried.
So exactly-once isn't necessarily one giant magical property.
It's often assembled from:
atomicity
+
stable identity
+
idempotency
+
durable state
+
retry
+
deduplication
