41. The hardest case: external side effects
Suppose:
Kafka
 ↓
Java
 ↓
DB
 ↓
Payment API
There is no single local transaction spanning:
Kafka
+
DB
+
Payment API
You need a strategy.
Possible designs include:
Strategy A — external API supports idempotency
P123 → payment API
Retry is safe.
Strategy B — use a transactional provider/ledger
Business operation becomes durable and reconciled.
Strategy C — asynchronous workflow
Instead of:
