Local DB transactions solve:
business state + deduplication record
External idempotency solves:
repeated calls to external systems
________________________________________
52. The most important distinction of Lesson 4
If you remember only one thing:
Exactly-once execution is about how many times code runs. Exactly-once effect is about how many times the world changes.
Those are radically different guarantees.
For example:
Kafka:
    delivery = 3

Java:
    execution = 3

PostgreSQL:
    transaction attempts = 3

Business effect:
    1
That can be a perfectly designed system.
________________________________________
53. Now the uncomfortable question
Suppose your architecture is:
Kafka
 ↓
Java
 ↓
PostgreSQL
 ↓
REST API
 ↓
Email
and you make:
