6. At-least-once does NOT mean "the broker sends duplicates"
This distinction is subtle.
At-least-once means:
If the system accepts a message for delivery, it attempts to ensure that the consumer gets it at least once, but the same message may be delivered more than once.
Duplicates can arise from many failure scenarios.
For example:
Broker
   |
   | M
   v
Consumer
   |
   | process
   v
Database
   |
   | COMMIT
   v
Consumer
   |
   | ACK
   X
