The business effect already happened.
But the broker doesn't know that.
So:
Broker's perspective:

M
 ↓
not acknowledged
 ↓
retry
The broker isn't necessarily "wrong."
It has incomplete information.
This leads to a deeper distributed-systems principle:
A participant cannot always distinguish "the operation failed" from "the operation succeeded but the response was lost."
