8. Three delivery models more deeply
At-most-once
Typical sequence:
receive
   ↓
ACK
   ↓
process
If processing fails:
message is gone
Therefore:
0 or 1 processing attempts
Advantages:
•	low duplicate risk 
•	simpler consumer state 
•	often lower latency 
Disadvantage:
•	messages can be lost 
Useful when:
