9. At-least-once
Typical sequence:
receive
   ↓
process
   ↓
ACK
If processing succeeds but ACK fails:
       process
          ↓
       success
          ↓
       ACK fails
          ↓
      redelivery
          ↓
       process
Therefore:
1 or more processing attempts
Advantages:
•	much lower risk of losing accepted messages 
•	good fit for financial/business workflows 
•	failures tend to become retries rather than silent loss 
Disadvantage:
Your consumer must tolerate duplicates.
This is an extremely important architectural consequence.
At-least-once isn't just a broker configuration.
It imposes a requirement on your application:
