public void handle(OrderCreated event) {

    orderRepository.updateStatus(...);

    paymentClient.charge(...);
}
The database transaction can potentially make:
DB operation
atomic with other DB operations.
But it cannot automatically roll back:
paymentClient.charge()
if the remote payment service already accepted the request.
So you have:
DB transaction boundary
       |
       |---- database
       |
       X---- external world
This is why distributed systems increasingly use concepts such as:
