12. A useful mental model: ownership of truth
When reasoning about delivery semantics, ask:
Who knows what?
Suppose:
Broker                    Consumer                  DB
  |                          |                       |
  | M                        |                       |
  |------------------------->|                       |
  |                          | UPDATE               |
  |                          |---------------------->|
  |                          |                       |
  |                          |<------ COMMIT --------|
  |                          |                       |
  |                          | ACK                   |
  |<-------------------------|                       |
After the DB commit but before the ACK reaches the broker:
DB knows:
    operation succeeded

Consumer knows:
    operation succeeded

Broker thinks:
    operation may not have succeeded
Therefore broker retries.
This is not necessarily a bug.
The broker simply doesn't have the same knowledge as the DB.
That gives you:
DB truth ≠ broker knowledge
and duplicates emerge naturally.
