13. Delivery semantics vs failure semantics
Another important distinction.
Suppose a broker says:
"At-least-once delivery."
That does not mean:
your business operation will definitely happen
It means something closer to:
the messaging system will attempt delivery
without permanently discarding the message merely because
a delivery attempt failed.
Your consumer can still do:
try {
    process(message);
} catch (Exception e) {
    // bad handling
}
and effectively lose the message depending on the broker/consumer protocol.
So delivery semantics are a system property, but correct implementation requires cooperation between:
producer
broker
consumer
application
storage
