At-least-once doesn't promise that your code executes once; it asks you to make repeated execution safe.
And that idea is going to reappear throughout distributed systems—in Kafka, queues, retries, RPC, payment systems, outbox/inbox patterns, sagas, leader failover, and eventually exactly-once discussions.

